      "message": "I\u0027m starting to question whether we really want/need our own enums here or if we should just save the VkFormatFeatureFlags. Like for the texurable, I could see the benefit of supporting formats that can\u0027t be linearly sampled, so we just downgrade them to using nearest if linear is requested. We\u0027re already fine with downgrading mip sampling if we don\u0027t have mips.\n\nIt would mean that if we want to internally create something internally that is renderable we\u0027ll additionally have to add the check for sampled support each time (since that\u0027s what we in skia assume).\n\nBut it leaves us more flexible to check additional format features later in arbitrary combinations if needed.",
